From 46293f0b995325f416587eae03e040c7aeb9d1a8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Iaroslav Voitovych <yaroslav.voytovych@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 05:47:33 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Bluetooth: hci_conn: hold a reused SCO connection for its
 caller

Since commit 06149746e720 ("Bluetooth: hci_conn: Add support for
linking multiple hcon"), hci_connect_sco() takes no hold on the SCO
connection for its caller when the connection is reused: the only hold
comes from hci_conn_link(), which returns the existing link without
taking one. Since commit 8a5b0135d4a5 ("Bluetooth: SCO: fix race
conditions in sco_sock_connect()"), sco_connect() drops the caller's
hold when sco_chan_add() fails.

Together, a second connect() to a device whose SCO link is up drops the
hold of the socket that owns the link: sco_chan_add() fails with EBUSY,
the hold is dropped, hci_conn_timeout() then finds none left, and the
link of the first socket is disconnected.

Take the hold when the link exists. The ACL hold that hci_connect_acl()
took is redundant then, as the existing link owns one, and would keep
the ACL connection up after the SCO connection is gone, so drop it.

Fixes: 8a5b0135d4a5 ("Bluetooth: SCO: fix race conditions in sco_sock_connect()")
Signed-off-by: Iaroslav Voitovych <yaroslav.voytovych@gmail.com>
---
 net/bluetooth/hci_conn.c | 17 +++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/net/bluetooth/hci_conn.c b/net/bluetooth/hci_conn.c
index 8a20ccdf618c7..51651b3b312b6 100644
--- a/net/bluetooth/hci_conn.c
+++ b/net/bluetooth/hci_conn.c
@@ -1919,11 +1919,20 @@ struct hci_conn *hci_connect_sco(struct hci_dev *hdev, int type, bdaddr_t *dst,
 		return ERR_PTR(-ECONNABORTED);
 	}
 
-	link = hci_conn_link(acl, sco);
-	if (!link) {
+	if (sco->link) {
+		/* The existing link already owns the hold on the ACL, and the
+		 * caller needs its own hold on the SCO connection, which
+		 * hci_conn_link() only takes for a new link.
+		 */
 		hci_conn_drop(acl);
-		hci_conn_drop(sco);
-		return ERR_PTR(-ENOLINK);
+		hci_conn_hold(sco);
+	} else {
+		link = hci_conn_link(acl, sco);
+		if (!link) {
+			hci_conn_drop(acl);
+			hci_conn_drop(sco);
+			return ERR_PTR(-ENOLINK);
+		}
 	}
 
 	sco->setting = setting;
-- 
